200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (Project Brief: Child, Early, and Forced Marriage and Unions represent a profound violation of human rights that disproportionately impacts adolescent girls. It is rooted in deep-seated patriarchal norms, economic hardship, systemic gender inequality, and gaps in formal education. It deprives young individuals of their fundamental bodily autonomy, safety, and future potential.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (While multi-sectoral support is necessary for those already impacted, prevention is the primary path to ending it by stopping early unions before their occur breaks the cycle of intergenerational poverty, reduces maternal health complications, and keeps girls in school. This executive summary outlines a multi-layered preventative strategy designed to eliminate the root drivers of child marriage by empowering adolescent girls, transforming social norms, alleviating economic pressures, and reinforcing protective legal systems. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
