<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (Sunita, a 26-year-old mother from a small village in Namkum, faced severe financial distress after a failed harvest. When an unregistered agent arrived promising a high-paying domestic job in a distant city, Sunita felt she had no choice but to leave. Like many in her village, she was unaware of the legal requirements for labor migration or the risks of trafficking.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (Before Sunita could depart, she attended an awareness session hosted by the Safe Migration Vigilance Committee, established under the British Asian Trust project. It helped understand the Mandatory registration under labor laws, How to verify the legitimacy of migration agents, Claiming social security schemes to provide financial stability at home.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
